                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b906979a-7c18-3f38-ac4a-8c2b80599862",
                        "entry_id": "7db2859f-4b5b-32a1-b209-22a698f79674",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A boy servant, or page."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial",
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2836543-a5d1-47f3-a6b7-0ef2ade6fc79",
                                "sense_id": "b906979a-7c18-3f38-ac4a-8c2b80599862",
                                "text": "A Custum' Us officer knows what to do with his Buttons, \"said the Jack , repeating the obnoxious word with the greatest contempt , “when they comes betwixt him and his own light[…]\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f9c5c57f-d6c9-31f2-9939-ba99e8d54f02",
                        "entry_id": "7db2859f-4b5b-32a1-b209-22a698f79674",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A policeman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ebbb39d-abb3-4031-91ac-af4ffa96d70d",
                                "sense_id": "f9c5c57f-d6c9-31f2-9939-ba99e8d54f02",
                                "text": "‘Go ahead, call the buttons. You'll get a big reaction from it.’"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f5213e8e-e16d-30e5-b0cc-f7d06081dde6",
                        "entry_id": "7db2859f-4b5b-32a1-b209-22a698f79674",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of marbles (“sanity; mental faculties”)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf5c8b38-eb01-4bf6-a46f-3632256ed4c8",
                                "sense_id": "f5213e8e-e16d-30e5-b0cc-f7d06081dde6",
                                "text": "And we've got that other boy now, Ganesh something, I met him once, and I didn't understand a word he was saying, but the child seems to have all his buttons."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "31a022a9-8f95-4082-9bf3-4ec5f7767bf1",
                                "sense_id": "f5213e8e-e16d-30e5-b0cc-f7d06081dde6",
                                "text": "That night in his room before he'd left for New Orleans, Lewis had behaved like he didn't have all his buttons."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e021817f-e916-42e8-84aa-4e3798e09af1",
                                "sense_id": "f5213e8e-e16d-30e5-b0cc-f7d06081dde6",
                                "text": "In the quaint vernacular of old Dad Peppin, Zion Jore might not have all his buttons, but he had more of what he did have than most men—more imagination to conceive a plot, more daring to carry it out, no fear to hamper him, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9bb385c6-4980-3afd-8cb4-5ee2923dc423",
                        "entry_id": "7db2859f-4b5b-32a1-b209-22a698f79674",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A small South African plant of the genus Conophytum, with button-like succulent leaves covering its exterior."
                        ],
